[_] Specify metric references and targets on objectives =objective-metrics $DECIDED 2026-11-04 (Darrion): a ClearHead objective can name a metric and a target; comfortable because Ossie is an open format. Darrion also wants composed metrics, e.g. percent overdue = overdue actions / open actions * 100, which Ossie forbids (no metric may reference another). Context: the layers discussion in assistant's log 2026-11-04 (records, implementations per source, meaning entries, intentions, views). Open: the composition format and where metric entries live. Spec change: Darrion approves the text. First proof is assistant's =compute-metrics, not this spec.  DECIDED 2026-11-04 (Darrion): composed metrics are arithmetic over metric ids (numbers, references, + - * /, parentheses), with every input computed at the same as-of time and scope, and rollups composed at the requested grain. Division by zero is empty by default; a metric may declare when_empty (percent overdue declares 0). Darrion first chose 0 everywhere, then took the point that 0 misleads for ratios like conversion with no data.$ !3 ^2026-11-04T06:20 %2026-11-04T07:44 #01a1a537-c5b7-78d1-bb47-3a22e1d484ca
