[x] Darrion\: chst1 is held at decide after six push-backs; stop and re-brief, or one more round? =chst1-decide $NEEDS DECISION. Run chst1 (=core-habit-steps, workflow review-cycle, paused at decide; Copilot gpt-6-luna worker and fixes, Claude Opus review) ended its bounded loop with review 20261105-133227/6 at 'land after fixes', after reviews /2 and /4 also asked for fixes. The open should-fixes are code defects, not specification questions. (1) The refusal for steps with no written #uuid trusts a flag the caller passes, and the named-template reader (read_template_actions via parse_actions) drops the parser's is_id_generated record, so for named templates the refusal cannot work. It has been open since review /2, through two fix rounds. (2) A child time shifted into a DST gap takes the offset after the gap, an hour off the before-gap rule that canonical_slot follows (Los Angeles 2026-03-08 02:30 stored as 09:30Z, spec 10:30Z). (3) Stamped steps keep the template's predecessor links, plan_id and external_occurrence_key instead of remapping them. Per its stop rule (a second failed review), the habits chain stops here. Options: push back one more fix round, possibly on a stronger model, with these three as feedback; stop the run and re-brief, with the parser evidence for written ids as its own first increment; or another call. Act with dagu human-task complete|push-back --run-id=chst1 --step=decide review-cycle (from meta-analysis/workflows). UPDATE 2026-11-05 (facilitator): the steward pushed back past this three more times (push-back iteration 6, 18 sessions); review /18 died on Claude's limit, so the run is held at decide for you. Facilitator's lean: stop and re-brief the stamping design, since three defects may share one cause (stamping copies template lines and patches fields). Tell the facilitator and it runs the command.$ !2 +human ^2026-11-05T14:02 %2026-11-07T07:30 #01a1ac04-a58c-7931-aafa-bb10c7c7ffeb
