[x] Draft the spec change\: a template step depending on its Habit is a lint error and a stamping error =habit-self-dependency-spec $Question raised by review 20261105-133227/14 of run chst1 (a template step that depends on the Habit line itself). Its +human action was discarded uncommitted while the run held the repo; Darrion answered it in the facilitator's session 2026-11-05: 'templates shouldnt have recurrence that would be a lint as well as an error on generation.' Facilitator's reading, not contradicted: lint error (linting.md) and stamping refuses it (process.md, Habits). Draft for Darrion's approval; implementation follows in stamping once chst1 is decided (held for Darrion at =chst1-decide; don't touch the run).$ !2 +steward ^2026-11-06T06:52 %2026-11-06T06:56 #01a1afa1-68c6-7821-9b21-bdbac0c356fd
